:db/id #edb/ref 17592186071349} {:answer/id #uuid "e71abec1-af90-564e-96cc-65f749dff99a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186071350} {:answer/id #uuid "f9bd14c8-f201-5c70-ba77-5489006197a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186071351} {:answer/id #uuid "30891c0a-e32e-5e99-9826-2629f5f5792b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186071352} {:answer/id #uuid "424e6c76-ef65-55f4-bb2c-05129500785f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186071353}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "831b8a12-3240-5543-8f0b-63a066174430" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186071349} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ff0f62d-b46f-5fed-abea-e9c339cbff76" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186071348}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5c71bd6b-b9a3-5587-89f4-a14a2c760bc2" :question/math-academy-id "q-5179" :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $p-q?$\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3p &=15 \\\\ p+2q &=9.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. It doesn't matter which equation we pick first, so we choose the easiest one. In this case, the first equation looks like the easiest.\n\nUsing the first equation, we can isolate $p$ by dividing both sides of the equation by $3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3p & =15 \\\\ p & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $p=5$ into $p+2q=9,$ then we can find the value of $q:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p+2q & =9 \\\\ (5)+2q & =9 \\\\ 2q & =4 \\\\ q & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $p=5,\\,q=2.$ So,\n\n$$\np-q=5-2=3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233560 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d447476e-6786-52c0-9a5b-aa6aa6b42f96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232246}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d447476e-6786-52c0-9a5b-aa6aa6b42f96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232246} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6f81397-282c-55bf-a574-31b7a7eb6872" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232245} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0d9ee9f-e333-5485-a7ba-ff333f3a6931" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "600" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232248}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0d9ee9f-e333-5485-a7ba-ff333f3a6931" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "600" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232248} :answer-field/id #uuid "e81a89a6-5e45-5c38-944f-815f8eebc873" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232247}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ba03c851-f080-5b98-bcba-fc2174ffc663" :question/math-academy-id "q-167194" :question/problem "The coefficients $a$ and $b$ also satisfy the equation $20b+400a=7\\,200.$ Find the values of $a$ and $b.$\n\n$a\\,=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$b\\,=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "We have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}b &=480-10a \\\\ 20b+400a &=7\\,200\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nNotice that the first equation is already solved for $b:$\n\n$$\nb=480-10a\n$$\n\nSo, we replace $b$ in the second equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20b+400a & =7\\,200 \\\\ 20(480-10a)+400a & =7\\,200 \\\\ 9\\,600-200a+400a & =7\\,200 \\\\ 9\\,600+200a & =7\\,200 \\\\ 200a & =-2\\,400 \\\\ a & =-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=-12$ into $b=480-10a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =480-10(-12) \\\\ b & =600\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=-12,\\,b=600.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233567 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25f6ebe2-11a4-50a4-afb6-e54166d6b757" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232262}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25f6ebe2-11a4-50a4-afb6-e54166d6b757" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232262} :answer-field/id #uuid "d89c06a2-d40d-59be-aba2-b51cfcb77eb2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232261} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81d5e96b-1699-54bb-87d3-abe3b34a48dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "320" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232264}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81d5e96b-1699-54bb-87d3-abe3b34a48dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "320" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232264} :answer-field/id #uuid "80788b1d-1ccd-5c42-ae32-41ab3f383746" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232263}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d104504e-e7b5-56df-8154-499bbc1d3f80" :question/math-academy-id "q-167210" :question/problem "The coefficients $a$ and $b$ also satisfy the equation $30b+900a=6\\,000.$ Find the values of $a$ and $b.$\n\n$a\\,=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$b\\,=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "We have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}b &=240-20a \\\\ 30b+900a &=6\\,000\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nNotice that the first equation is already solved for $b:$\n\n$$\nb=240-20a\n$$\n\nSo, we replace $b$ in the second equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}30b+900a & =6\\,000 \\\\ 30(240-20a)+900a & =6\\,000 \\\\ 7\\,200-600a+900a & =6\\,000 \\\\ 7\\,200+300a & =6\\,000 \\\\ 300a & =-1\\,200 \\\\ a & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=-4$ into $b=240-20a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =240-20(-4) \\\\ b & =320\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=-4,\\,b=320.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233574 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74b8ef99-22cc-5e49-9884-ae62824c5059" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232278}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74b8ef99-22cc-5e49-9884-ae62824c5059" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232278} :answer-field/id #uuid "194751b6-0ff6-5047-a6e8-f7e3cfbe1451" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232277} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39731897-add5-5068-a83a-649fb0aa6e48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232280}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39731897-add5-5068-a83a-649fb0aa6e48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232280} :answer-field/id #uuid "03a21b91-803e-51b3-8b0d-859c1f623d17" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232279}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6afc1799-60d6-5f69-94a5-994731079a93" :question/math-academy-id "q-167226" :question/problem "The coefficients $a$ and $b$ also satisfy the equation $70a+9b=600.$ Find the values of $a$ and $b.$\n\n$a\\,=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$b\\,=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "We have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}b &=75-5a \\\\ 70a+9b &=600\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nNotice that the first equation is already solved for $b:$\n\n$$\nb=75-5a\n$$\n\nSo, we replace $b$ in the second equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}70a+9b & =600 \\\\ 70a+9(75-5a) & =600 \\\\ 70a+675-45a & =600 \\\\ 25a+675 & =600 \\\\ 25a & =-75 \\\\ a & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=-3$ into $b=75-5a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =75-5(-3) \\\\ b & =90\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=-3,\\,b=90.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496226 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51c5dada-d996-51cf-94d1-ca897ceda4c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495696}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51c5dada-d996-51cf-94d1-ca897ceda4c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495696} :answer-field/id #uuid "da300820-d65a-54b5-a122-648e1be4ca42" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496194} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0db68d80-560b-5294-a3e9-812966c11801" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495542}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0db68d80-560b-5294-a3e9-812966c11801" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495542} :answer-field/id #uuid "e16e42d5-5e57-5702-bb36-98fb0bad0dd6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496198}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "07b5302b-d797-5328-827e-aa28a460f929" :question/math-academy-id "q-181149" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4u-6v &=-3 \\\\ u &=-v-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the solution $(u,v)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$(u,v)=($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. It so happens that the second equation is already solved for $u:$\n\n$$\nu=-v-2\n$$\n\nSo, we replace $u$ with $-v-2$ in the first equation and solve for $v:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4u-6v & =-3 \\\\ 4(-v-2)-6v & =-3 \\\\ -4v-8-6v & =-3 \\\\ -10v & =5 \\\\ v & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $v=-\\frac{1}{2}$ into $u=-v-2,$ then we can find the value of $u:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =-v-2 \\\\ u & =-\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)-2 \\\\ u & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $u=-\\frac{3}{2},\\,v=-\\frac{1}{2},$ which can be expressed as $(-\\frac{3}{2},-\\frac{1}{2}).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496252 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ed3f880-96ed-5fd6-824f-be81fbff3e25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495753} {:answer/id #uuid "92cf3e39-98db-564f-a3c5-ad104dff9377" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495833} {:answer/id #uuid "adefce60-eb41-5a32-906f-e3cd671a3daa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495899} {:answer/id #uuid "b6612f39-f352-56c1-817b-399df43c996f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495919} {:answer/id #uuid "e81c2d81-0ae0-51a8-90a5-645bcd295610" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496022}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ed3f880-96ed-5fd6-824f-be81fbff3e25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495753} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca46e4e1-5150-5d40-98c3-33efe3175aed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496180}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "498d2b3f-6756-59df-bd3d-256bb722b0aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-112214" :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $y-x?$\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}21x-9y &=0 \\\\ 5y-15x+10 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We number the equations so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}21x-9y &=0 && \\,\\,(1) \\\\ 5y-15x+10 &=0 && \\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $(2),$ we can isolate $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5y-15x+10 & =0 \\\\ 5y & =15x-10 \\\\ y & =3x-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $3x-2$  into equation $(1)$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}21x-9y & =0 \\\\ 21x-9(3x-2) & =0 \\\\ 21x-27x+18 & =0 \\\\ -6x+18 & =0 \\\\ 18 & =6x \\\\ 3 & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $x=3$ into $y=3x-2,$ then we can find the value of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3x-2 \\\\ y & =3(3)-2 \\\\ y & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=3,\\,y=7.$ So,\n\n$$\ny-x=7-3=4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496255 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "001fa025-6178-5ba4-b287-f99d23255489" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "001fa025-6178-5ba4-b287-f99d23255489" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495509} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c44ea3f-ae01-5f06-b1d9-d8a1d677d43e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496138} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e2cf528e-9238-53c7-ac72-2595f6c61117" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496013}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2cf528e-9238-53c7-ac72-2595f6c61117" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496013} :answer-field/id #uuid "d81fe473-caed-55d0-ae06-56890f9a6929" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496191}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "4c3907fe-c83e-5bd5-ac54-297aa503451b" :question/math-academy-id "q-181175" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+y &=-4 \\\\ x-3y &=-8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the solution $(x,y)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$(x,y)=($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. It doesn't matter which equation we pick first, so we choose the easiest one. In this case, the second equation looks like the easiest.\n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $x$ by adding $3y$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\nx=3y-8\n$$\n\nSo, we replace $x$ with $3y-8$ in the first equation and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+y & =-4 \\\\ -2(3y-8)+y & =-4 \\\\ -6y+16+y & =-4 \\\\ -5y & =-20 \\\\ y & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $y=4$ into $x=3y-8,$ then we can find the value of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =3y-8 \\\\ x & =3(4)-8 \\\\ x & =12-8 \\\\ x & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=4,\\,y=4,$ which can be expressed as $(4,4).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496314 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff409c69-65be-5db8-9082-449cc256ae35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496070}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff409c69-65be-5db8-9082-449cc256ae35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496070} :answer-field/id #uuid "d502feb6-12a4-5b5d-a239-789af82850e4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496187} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be1f5640-6243-5fce-a7c7-5b82c5d69ef4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495929}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be1f5640-6243-5fce-a7c7-5b82c5d69ef4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495929} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef8a675b-4a10-5910-adfc-f84ccbe5facf" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496207}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d389f84f-6df2-5d57-9702-acb625d9c80f" :question/math-academy-id "q-181207" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3p-6q &=-18 \\\\ 4p+3q+2 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the solution $(p,q)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$(p,q)=($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "We number the equations so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3p-6q &=-18 && \\,\\,(1) \\\\ 4p+3q+2 &=0 && \\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $(1),$ we can solve for $p$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3p-6q & =-18 \\\\ 3p & =6q-18 \\\\ p & =2q-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $p=2q-6$ into equation $(2)$ and solve for $q:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(2q-6)+3q+2 & =0 \\\\ 8q-24+3q+2 & =0 \\\\ 11q & =22 \\\\ q & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $q=2$ into equation $(1),$ then we can find the value of $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3p-6(2) & =-18 \\\\ 3p-12 & =-18 \\\\ 3p & =-6 \\\\ p & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $p=-2,\\,q=2,$ which can be expressed as $(-2,2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497411 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "951ed025-e4b5-517b-830a-a3da54b9c6e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "128" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496968}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "951ed025-e4b5-517b-830a-a3da54b9c6e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "128" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496968} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c523c48-ec60-5fa0-9eec-5d07498f1571" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497224} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eebbe5cc-91ee-5b03-9257-cc5f956ce523" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2240" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497171}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eebbe5cc-91ee-5b03-9257-cc5f956ce523" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2240" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497171} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb7943f0-b18a-5a1c-9e1c-77a8a3b53234" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497319}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ededc7bf-b310-5714-a047-930df525362b" :question/math-academy-id "q-166843" :question/problem "The pastry shop's total cost and revenue per month (in dollars) from selling cakes can be modeled by the equations $y=1\\,600+5n$ and $y=64+17n,$ respectively, where $n$ is the number of cakes sold. \n\nSolve the system below using the substitution method to find the exact number of cakes needed to break even and the revenue made.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=1\\,600+5n \\\\ y &=64+17n\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe pastry shop breaks even when$\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\,$cakes are produced. \n\nThe revenue made when selling this number of cakes is$\\,$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\,$dollars." :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nNotice that $y$ is isolated in the first equation. Therefore, we can replace $y$ with $1\\,600+5n$ in the second equation and solve for $n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =64+17n \\\\ 1\\,600+5n & =64+17n \\\\ 1\\,600+5n-64 & =64+17n-64 \\\\ 1\\,536+5n & =17n \\\\ 1\\,536+5n-5n & =17n-5n \\\\ 1\\,536 & =12n \\\\ \\frac{1\\,536}{12} & =\\frac{12n}{12} \\\\ 128 & =n \\\\ n & =128\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $n=128$ into $y=64+17n$, then we can find the value of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &=64+17(128)=2\\,240\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the solution to the system of equations is $n=128$ and $y=2\\,240.$\nTherefore, the pastry shop breaks even when $128$ units are produced, and the revenue made when selling this number of units is $2\\,240$ dollars."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186503753 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e2466bb-be73-57a5-a448-e2ae0ba60c2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503039}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e2466bb-be73-57a5-a448-e2ae0ba60c2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503039} :answer-field/id #uuid "163d9f6a-4519-5200-83a3-6d401cb44c91" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503523} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13a5bcc9-bf29-57f7-9c4f-15fe366965e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "540" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503022}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13a5bcc9-bf29-57f7-9c4f-15fe366965e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "540" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503022} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d99e451-ff6c-54c5-be9e-d8c096902ab9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503554}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ee041a5d-3530-58d3-9ad7-acdf10ca4984" :question/math-academy-id "q-166761" :question/problem "Mary wonders where and when they'd meet if Sam left home $3.8$ minutes earlier and walked with a speed of $50$ meters per minute. She finds that the distance $d$ from home they'd meet can be modeled using the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}d+60t &=960 \\\\ d-50t &=190.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time (in minutes) since Mary left the community park.\n\nMary and Sam would meet$\\,$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$minutes after Mary left the community park.\n\nMary and Sam would meet at a distance of $\\,$\n{{field-2}}$\\,$meters from home." :question/worked-solution "To solve the given system of linear equations, we will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. It doesn't matter which equation we pick first, so we choose the easiest one. In this case, the second equation looks like the easiest.\n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $d$ adding to both sides of the equation $50t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d-50t &=190 \\\\ d &=190+50t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we replace $d$ with $190+50t$ in the first equation and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d+60t=960 \\\\ (190+50t)+60t & =960 \\\\ 190+110t & =960 \\\\ 110t & =960-190 \\\\ 110t & =770 \\\\ t & =\\frac{770}{110} \\\\ t & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, they would have met after $t=7$ minutes.\n\nIf we substitute $t=7$ into $d=190+50t$, we can find the value of $d:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =190+50t \\\\  & =190+50(7) \\\\  & =540\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, they meet at a distance of $540$ meters from home."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505001 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f73540b-32d9-5ee1-94a3-da5422f97d77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\dfrac{13}{4}, y = \\dfrac{19}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505009} {:answer/id #uuid "44122e05-b69e-592e-bb1a-ad25db4cd762" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 29, y = 13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505020} {:answer/id #uuid "5db18aeb-0e38-56e7-a0bf-c756cfb1cfbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\dfrac{19}{2}, y = \\dfrac{13}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505029} {:answer/id #uuid "b6a8c0bb-a01c-535c-9c2e-ae6134e38e7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 17, y = 7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505060} {:answer/id #uuid "c5afbb05-60ff-501b-9b83-4d3e11b87d54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\dfrac{43}{10}, y = -\\dfrac{13}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505068}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5db18aeb-0e38-56e7-a0bf-c756cfb1cfbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\dfrac{19}{2}, y = \\dfrac{13}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505029} :answer-field/id #uuid "815fa2e4-c3a2-5a69-900d-b75d009dd0e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505043}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "019711ee-80ff-5bba-9b3e-59b676517b88" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6x - 8y - 31 &=0 \\\\ 2x - 4y - 6 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Sometimes, it's handy to assign a number to each equation in a system, so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6x - 8y - 31 &=0 && (1) \\\\ 2x - 4y - 6 &=0 && (2)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $\\color{blue}(2)$, we can solve for $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 2x - 4y - 6 &= 0 \\\\ 2x - 4y &= 6 \\\\ 2x &= 6 + 4y \\\\ x &= \\dfrac{6 + 4y}{2} \\\\ x &= 3 + 2y \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=3+2y$ into equation $\\color{red}(1)$ and solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 6x - 8y - 31 &= 0 \\\\ 6(3 + 2y) - 8y - 31 &= 0 \\\\ 18 + 12y - 8y - 31 &= 0 \\\\ -13 + 4y &= 0 \\\\ 4y &= 13 \\\\ y &= \\dfrac{13}{4} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{13}{4}\n$$\n\ninto equation $\\color{red}(1)$, then we can find the value of $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 6x - 8y - 31 &= 0 \\\\ 6x - 8\\left(\\dfrac{13}{4}\\right) - 31 &= 0 \\\\ 6x - 26 - 31 &= 0 \\\\ 6x - 57 &= 0 \\\\ 6x &= 57 \\\\ x &= \\dfrac{19}{2} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=\\dfrac{19}{2}$ and\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{13}{4}\n$$\n\n, which can be written as\n\n$$\n\\left(\\dfrac{19}{2},\\dfrac{13}{4}\\right)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505002 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bf84d08-1dca-5218-a07d-994057aff387" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a = 6, b = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505013} {:answer/id #uuid "528de811-2b56-5a74-8d2e-07cb5fc3b4d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a = -11, b = -6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505027} {:answer/id #uuid "5db52a37-23c1-5600-9bdb-08a8c2b96623" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a = 1, b = 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505030} {:answer/id #uuid "c22e9a45-ce60-5743-bfae-86b5026038eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a = 31, b = 36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505065} {:answer/id #uuid "d5b41247-404b-570f-87a4-1f5c8538e314" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a = -\\dfrac{27}{5}, b = \\dfrac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505074}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5db52a37-23c1-5600-9bdb-08a8c2b96623" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a = 1, b = 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505030} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a812c87-5420-54d1-b5e9-1d7596284773" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505024}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "037d812f-9cb8-5f58-959c-05369edfd299" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}7a - 8b + 41 &=0 \\\\ 4a - 4b + 20 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Sometimes, it's handy to assign a number to each equation in a system, so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}7a - 8b + 41 &=0 && (1) \\\\ 4a - 4b + 20 &=0 && (2)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $\\color{blue}(2)$, we can solve for $a$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 4a - 4b + 20 &= 0 \\\\ 4a - 4b &= -20 \\\\ 4a &= -20 + 4b \\\\ a &= \\dfrac{-20 + 4b}{4} \\\\ a &= -5 + b \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $a=-5+b$ into equation $\\color{red}(1)$ and solve for $b$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 7a - 8b + 41 &= 0 \\\\ 7(-5 + b) - 8b + 41 &= 0 \\\\ -35 + 7b - 8b + 41 &= 0 \\\\ 6 - b &= 0 \\\\ -b &= -6 \\\\ b &= 6 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute\n\n$$\nb=6\n$$\n\ninto equation $\\color{red}(1)$, then we can find the value of $a$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 7a - 8b + 41 &= 0 \\\\ 7a - 8\\left(6\\right) + 41 &= 0 \\\\ 7a - 48 + 41 &= 0 \\\\ 7a - 7 &= 0 \\\\ 7a &= 7 \\\\ a &= 1 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=1$ and\n\n$$\nb=6\n$$\n\n, which can be written as\n\n$$\n\\left(1,6\\right)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505004 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e7cdf5a-5a46-5390-8a6a-5ed18ae9d9f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = -1, y = -5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505018} {:answer/id #uuid "49c9a908-228f-59d5-8607-095ccbac281a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = -8, y = 9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505023} {:answer/id #uuid "7101e81a-dd60-5923-8f05-ece2ae2d5dee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = -5, y = -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505039} {:answer/id #uuid "d9612a71-c4c9-5df6-a1f8-4d50c4e71893" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\dfrac{5}{2}, y = -12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505076} {:answer/id #uuid "de10306a-4f55-5205-b610-875a785ea3d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 2, y = -3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505079}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e7cdf5a-5a46-5390-8a6a-5ed18ae9d9f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = -1, y = -5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505018} :answer-field/id #uuid "f40c9b80-4cc9-5cb8-afa4-0371d87b467c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505088}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0b3f4cbe-31b3-5a2d-8c6e-81aafdba130b" :question/problem "Using the method of substitution, find the solution of\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x + y &=-7 \\\\ 2x - 3y &=13\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$." :question/worked-solution "Sometimes, it's handy to assign a number to each equation in a system, so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x + y + 7 &=0 && (1) \\\\ 2x - 3y - 13 &=0 && (2)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $\\color{blue}(1)$, we can solve for $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} y + 2x + 7 &= 0 \\\\ y + 2x &= -7 \\\\ y &= -7 - 2x \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $y=-7-2x$ into equation $\\color{red}(2)$ and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} -3y + 2x - 13 &= 0 \\\\ -3(-7 - 2x) + 2x - 13 &= 0 \\\\ 21 + 6x + 2x - 13 &= 0 \\\\ 8 + 8x &= 0 \\\\ 8x &= -8 \\\\ x &= -1 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute\n\n$$\nx=-1\n$$\n\ninto equation $\\color{red}(2)$, then we can find the value of $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} -3y + 2x - 13 &= 0 \\\\ -3y + 2\\left(-1\\right) - 13 &= 0 \\\\ -3y - 2 - 13 &= 0 \\\\ -3y - 15 &= 0 \\\\ -3y &= 15 \\\\ y &= -5 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $y=-5$ and\n\n$$\nx=-1\n$$\n\n, which can be written as\n\n$$\n\\left(-1,-5\\right)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505005 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "188de890-3550-53a3-ae4b-7aee43ba4d4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p = -\\dfrac{4}{5}, q = \\dfrac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505012} {:answer/id #uuid "6d5479ec-6dd9-59aa-b198-6622d2186e70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p = -\\dfrac{8}{3}, q = \\dfrac{14}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505037} {:answer/id #uuid "763b7950-8d3e-5755-9ce3-f22e1857cbd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p = -2, q = 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505041} {:answer/id #uuid "8bda9132-2104-519c-bd63-9eff3522c541" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p 