 - 8 &= 0 \\\\ 2u + 4v &= 8 \\\\ 2u &= 8 - 4v \\\\ u &= \\dfrac{8 - 4v}{2} \\\\ u &= 4 - 2v \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $u=4-2v$ into equation $\\color{red}(1)$ and solve for $v$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 3u - 10v - 24 &= 0 \\\\ 3(4 - 2v) - 10v - 24 &= 0 \\\\ 12 - 6v - 10v - 24 &= 0 \\\\ -12 - 16v &= 0 \\\\ -16v &= 12 \\\\ v &= -\\dfrac{3}{4} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute\n\n$$\nv=-\\dfrac{3}{4}\n$$\n\ninto equation $\\color{red}(1)$, then we can find the value of $u$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 3u - 10v - 24 &= 0 \\\\ 3u - 10\\left(-\\dfrac{3}{4}\\right) - 24 &= 0 \\\\ 3u + \\dfrac{15}{2} - 24 &= 0 \\\\ 3u - \\dfrac{33}{2} &= 0 \\\\ 3u &= \\dfrac{33}{2} \\\\ u &= \\dfrac{11}{2} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $u=\\dfrac{11}{2}$ and\n\n$$\nv=-\\dfrac{3}{4}\n$$\n\n, which can be written as\n\n$$\n\\left(\\dfrac{11}{2},-\\dfrac{3}{4}\\right)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505067 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f226940-943f-583c-bfad-7e0e457a4495" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = -2, y = 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505006} {:answer/id #uuid "555ddb93-7974-58de-ab26-661f601b92e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 8, y = -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505028} {:answer/id #uuid "64401688-65df-53f3-8d39-351c9d9e6764" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 40, y = -18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505033} {:answer/id #uuid "6e4da099-0ce4-5de2-b9ea-a991cd983ef7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\dfrac{152}{9}, y = -\\dfrac{58}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505038} {:answer/id #uuid "cf7e8244-2976-579c-bc22-7eba63d1400a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\dfrac{16}{3}, y = \\dfrac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505071}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "555ddb93-7974-58de-ab26-661f601b92e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 8, y = -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505028} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e4dec55-ce2d-5af5-9a72-496c649ac130" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505026}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c436498f-fd9e-57ef-8d83-36d474017d7b" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-9x - 9y + 54 &=0 \\\\ 4x + 8y - 16 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Sometimes, it's handy to assign a number to each equation in a system, so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-9x - 9y + 54 &=0 && (1) \\\\ 4x + 8y - 16 &=0 && (2)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $\\color{blue}(2)$, we can solve for $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 4x + 8y - 16 &= 0 \\\\ 4x + 8y &= 16 \\\\ 4x &= 16 - 8y \\\\ x &= \\dfrac{16 - 8y}{4} \\\\ x &= 4 - 2y \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=4-2y$ into equation $\\color{red}(1)$ and solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} -9x - 9y + 54 &= 0 \\\\ -9(4 - 2y) - 9y + 54 &= 0 \\\\ -36 + 18y - 9y + 54 &= 0 \\\\ 18 + 9y &= 0 \\\\ 9y &= -18 \\\\ y &= -2 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute\n\n$$\ny=-2\n$$\n\ninto equation $\\color{red}(1)$, then we can find the value of $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} -9x - 9y + 54 &= 0 \\\\ -9x - 9\\left(-2\\right) + 54 &= 0 \\\\ -9x + 18 + 54 &= 0 \\\\ -9x + 72 &= 0 \\\\ -9x &= -72 \\\\ x &= 8 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=8$ and\n\n$$\ny=-2\n$$\n\n, which can be written as\n\n$$\n\\left(8,-2\\right)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505080 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21558f44-0dc3-5110-86d8-087739b963cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 7, y = 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505016} {:answer/id #uuid "2a2a695b-0075-5418-984a-73a32e5438c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 2, y = 7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505017} {:answer/id #uuid "5ddccadf-36b4-5cfb-b0ee-35c46f4f5a8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\dfrac{85}{7}, y = \\dfrac{32}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505031} {:answer/id #uuid "c0951927-a913-5192-9133-898c36910349" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\dfrac{13}{3}, y = -\\dfrac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505064} {:answer/id #uuid "f38326ee-5794-566c-b7a6-3ec481868125" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 31, y = 14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505087}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21558f44-0dc3-5110-86d8-087739b963cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 7, y = 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505016} :answer-field/id #uuid "8913c7f5-e0f0-50ed-8a31-fc8d655919b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505045}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e37d0a68-8577-5a70-a5bd-f408d06259f5" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}7x - 7y - 35 &=0 \\\\ 2x - 4y - 6 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Sometimes, it's handy to assign a number to each equation in a system, so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}7x - 7y - 35 &=0 && (1) \\\\ 2x - 4y - 6 &=0 && (2)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $\\color{blue}(2)$, we can solve for $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 2x - 4y - 6 &= 0 \\\\ 2x - 4y &= 6 \\\\ 2x &= 6 + 4y \\\\ x &= \\dfrac{6 + 4y}{2} \\\\ x &= 3 + 2y \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=3+2y$ into equation $\\color{red}(1)$ and solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 7x - 7y - 35 &= 0 \\\\ 7(3 + 2y) - 7y - 35 &= 0 \\\\ 21 + 14y - 7y - 35 &= 0 \\\\ -14 + 7y &= 0 \\\\ 7y &= 14 \\\\ y &= 2 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute\n\n$$\ny=2\n$$\n\ninto equation $\\color{red}(1)$, then we can find the value of $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 7x - 7y - 35 &= 0 \\\\ 7x - 7\\left(2\\right) - 35 &= 0 \\\\ 7x - 14 - 35 &= 0 \\\\ 7x - 49 &= 0 \\\\ 7x &= 49 \\\\ x &= 7 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=7$ and\n\n$$\ny=2\n$$\n\n, which can be written as\n\n$$\n\\left(7,2\\right)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505081 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05d9c1d8-7776-59ee-ab3f-0c7ec5d99ad7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505003} {:answer/id #uuid "44ac7e7a-8cd6-5536-adaf-69acb445a0a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\dfrac{37}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505021} {:answer/id #uuid "4d5e58df-d87a-5d3b-8451-91e9e3f1757c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505025} {:answer/id #uuid "77b69005-e991-580b-b25e-307a1dd218c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505042} {:answer/id #uuid "92ad25d7-c40d-5066-bdbf-dd1acaadfdab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505049}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77b69005-e991-580b-b25e-307a1dd218c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505042} :answer-field/id #uuid "64e915ee-d4a5-507a-aa63-39fcbb83ebee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505035}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e7e74981-78de-5721-8c70-6b15d18904de" :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a - b$?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4b + 32 &=0 \\\\ 5a + 2b - 19 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $\\color{red}(1)$, we can solve for $b$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 4b + 32 &= 0 \\\\ 4b &= -32 \\\\ b &= -8 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $b=-8$ into equation $\\color{blue}(2)$ and solve for $a$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 5a + 2b - 19 &= 0 \\\\ 5a + 2\\left(-8\\right) - 19 &= 0 \\\\ 5a - 16 - 19 &= 0 \\\\ 5a &= 35 \\\\ a &= 7 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a - b = 7 - \\left(-8\\right) = 15$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505084 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c15ecbe-d346-5f65-915b-40b893526bce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = -62, y = 33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505014} {:answer/id #uuid "66049ae6-acb9-5ef1-9cbf-b5980d95fb61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\dfrac{9}{5}, y = -\\dfrac{11}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505036} {:answer/id #uuid "b8dc18ed-b3e2-5fe6-9ed6-a243f631ece2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\dfrac{33}{10}, y = -\\dfrac{13}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505061} {:answer/id #uuid "bcc54da3-d9e3-59a1-99b4-05f22aa87741" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\dfrac{31}{5}, y = -\\dfrac{11}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505063} {:answer/id #uuid "fab16b5f-e937-5c12-9738-1fe6637231e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = -\\dfrac{13}{5}, y = \\dfrac{33}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505091}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fab16b5f-e937-5c12-9738-1fe6637231e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = -\\dfrac{13}{5}, y = \\dfrac{33}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505091} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac43374e-aef2-5557-9421-83f8f3b1b206" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505056}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ed97dc9b-b6f4-5076-b3bb-6acac17b72a7" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-10x - 10y + 7 &=0 \\\\ 4x + 8y - 16 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Sometimes, it's handy to assign a number to each equation in a system, so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-10x - 10y + 7 &=0 && (1) \\\\ 4x + 8y - 16 &=0 && (2)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $\\color{blue}(2)$, we can solve for $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 4x + 8y - 16 &= 0 \\\\ 4x + 8y &= 16 \\\\ 4x &= 16 - 8y \\\\ x &= \\dfrac{16 - 8y}{4} \\\\ x &= 4 - 2y \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=4-2y$ into equation $\\color{red}(1)$ and solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} -10x - 10y + 7 &= 0 \\\\ -10(4 - 2y) - 10y + 7 &= 0 \\\\ -40 + 20y - 10y + 7 &= 0 \\\\ -33 + 10y &= 0 \\\\ 10y &= 33 \\\\ y &= \\dfrac{33}{10} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{33}{10}\n$$\n\ninto equation $\\color{red}(1)$, then we can find the value of $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} -10x - 10y + 7 &= 0 \\\\ -10x - 10\\left(\\dfrac{33}{10}\\right) + 7 &= 0 \\\\ -10x - 33 + 7 &= 0 \\\\ -10x - 26 &= 0 \\\\ -10x &= 26 \\\\ x &= -\\dfrac{13}{5} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-\\dfrac{13}{5}$ and\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{33}{10}\n$$\n\n, which can be written as\n\n$$\n\\left(-\\dfrac{13}{5},\\dfrac{33}{10}\\right)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508171 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d8c7e85-9744-56b8-ad17-eac57676bf8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508177} {:answer/id #uuid "8ad2f379-b802-5a78-8607-922e2d09a5cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508211} {:answer/id #uuid "8c480585-9da5-5f00-8620-6f9f4b8471e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508212} {:answer/id #uuid "eda2dc78-3b71-5603-99bc-d2a18246622d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508237} {:answer/id #uuid "f85f3e50-67d1-5429-9721-b01c743f8a4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508239}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f85f3e50-67d1-5429-9721-b01c743f8a4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508239} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f3454ce-d4fe-5e69-9c29-1cf7c10c083c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508208}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "01d4210c-99cb-5509-8003-8615f9f2d644" :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a - b$?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3a-3b &=-18 \\\\ -2a+b &=7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $b$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2a+b & =7 \\\\ b & =7+2a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $b=7+2a$ into the first equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a-3b & =-18 \\\\ 3a-3(7+2a) & =-18 \\\\ 3a-21-6a & =-18 \\\\ -3a-21 & =-18 \\\\ -3a & =3 \\\\ a & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=-1$ into $b=7+2a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =7+2(-1) \\\\ b & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a-b=-1-(5)=-6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508174 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d173c13-b0d2-5277-871e-ecb5b39a99ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d173c13-b0d2-5277-871e-ecb5b39a99ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508176} :answer-field/id #uuid "4806076d-709c-5c2f-9105-4634d0972c75" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508191} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cea1815-2688-56a2-b4ab-965679af5b0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508175}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1cea1815-2688-56a2-b4ab-965679af5b0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508175} :answer-field/id #uuid "aeabe89b-5ecb-5574-b4fc-226f206baafd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508225}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1814dd75-6dc3-5a88-93bf-56fa1a5ec858" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+5y &=21 \\\\ y &=x-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\nFind the solution $(x, y)$ to this system using the method of substitution.The solution is\n$($\n{{field-1}}\n$, $\n{{field-2}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nNotice that the second equation is already solved for $y:$\n\n$$\ny=x-3\n$$\n\nSo, we replace $y$ in the first equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+5y & =21 \\\\ x+5(x-3) & =21 \\\\ x+5x-15 & =21 \\\\ 6x-15 & =21 \\\\ 6x & =36 \\\\ x & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $x=6$ into $y=x-3,$ we can then find the value of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =(6)-3 \\\\ y & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=6,\\,y=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508179 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70c5addc-2f92-5b2d-9cb9-315d42c2eaf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508203} {:answer/id #uuid "9c57a785-864f-578d-a998-d06a760a82b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508219} {:answer/id #uuid "9dc1215d-6449-5646-8c6a-c29cc1fa3226" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508220} {:answer/id #uuid "a49ee6a6-f0da-5faa-b3bf-a70649b568f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508223} {:answer/id #uuid "ea6e4596-9bcf-59c6-a3cb-0242f006b8e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508234}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a49ee6a6-f0da-5faa-b3bf-a70649b568f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508223} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6ff3c1c-579d-56f9-8656-874b7f2727c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508232}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2e8faafd-e3ef-5205-a5d6-b458af26d97f" :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a - b$?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3a-2b &=2 \\\\ -3a+b &=8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $b$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3a+b & =8 \\\\ b & =8+3a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $b=8+3a$ into the first equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3a-2b & =2 \\\\ -3a-2(8+3a) & =2 \\\\ -3a-16-6a & =2 \\\\ -9a-16 & =2 \\\\ -9a & =18 \\\\ a & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=-2$ into $b=8+3a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =8+3(-2) \\\\ b & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a-b=-2-(2)=-4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508187 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3eb5050b-2f97-532e-b6c8-5866bcc9fa51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508188}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3eb5050b-2f97-532e-b6c8-5866bcc9fa51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508188} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac08740b-e844-58dd-baf4-40ef0b885178" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508224} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f39f41a-cfb3-5bf0-b58f-8d17841342c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{17}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508189}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f39f41a-cfb3-5bf0-b58f-8d17841342c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{17}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508189} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa771fca-d97d-5b82-add7-3f2815e11284" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508240}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "3db3cd07-1246-5ea5-a44f-5fee48dd9a13" :question/problem "Find the solution $(x,y)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+3y &=2 \\\\ 3x+y &=-5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution is $($ {{field-1}} $, $ {{field-2}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+y & =-5 \\\\ y & =-5-3x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $y=-5-3x$ into the first equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+3y & =2 \\\\ 3x+3(-5-3x) & =2 \\\\ 3x-15-9x & =2 \\\\ -6x-15 & =2 \\\\ -6x & =17 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{17}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $x=-\\frac{17}{6}$ into $y=-5-3x,$ we can then find the value of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-5-3\\left(-\\frac{17}{6}\\right) \\\\ y & =\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-\\frac{17}{6},\\,y=\\frac{7}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508204 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61123492-b1fa-52ea-a78d-92d15eb4799a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508201}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61123492-b1fa-52ea-a78d-92d15eb4799a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508201} :answer-field/id #uuid "00e813eb-39d3-591a-bc56-b776bdfd2316" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508170} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fc36be2-1ad6-5b03-b736-d29211c26e29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{16}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508194}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fc36be2-1ad6-5b03-b736-d29211c26e29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{16}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508194} :answer-field/id #uuid "84b6ed04-ec34-5023-a363-127985a3747a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508209}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "76c476e0-406c-5751-a806-f5cbe03fe610" :question/problem "Find the solution $(x,y)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x+4y &=8 \\\\ -2x+y &=6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution is $($ {{field-1}} $, $ {{field-2}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+y & =6 \\\\ y & =6+2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $y=6+2x$ into the first equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x+4y & =8 \\\\ -3x+4(6+2x) & =8 \\\\ -3x+24+8x & =8 \\\\ 5x+24 & =8 \\\\ 5x & =-16 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{16}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $x=-\\frac{16}{5}$ into $y=6+2x,$ we can then find the value of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =6+2\\left(-\\frac{16}{5}\\right) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-\\frac{16}{5},\\,y=-\\frac{2}{5}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508205 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b524116-52f0-5f16-ae76-c059374938ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508185} {:answer/id #uuid "7be0167d-61f1-500e-a6e6-d5a8f953e8c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508206} {:answer/id #uuid "904ce195-1201-5ff2-98fd-a1b9b5f6be03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508213} {:answer/id #uuid "979f6cea-60ca-5f62-beef-5756f8383e4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508217} {:answer/id #uuid "cfb36f0e-5371-55ee-b6e5-d11c77737dc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508230}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b524116-52f0-5f16-ae76-c059374938ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508185} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a85b03b-c3ea-57e4-a844-98bb80d07f7c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508193}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7afeeb08-8b8f-54f1-86b4-033f592e20d8" :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a - b$?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-5a+2b &=9 \\\\ -3a+b &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $b$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3a+b & =3 \\\\ b & =3+3a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $b=3+3a$ into the first equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5a+2b & =9 \\\\ -5a+2(3+3a) & =9 \\\\ -5a+6+6a & =9 \\\\ a+6 & =9 \\\\ a & =3 \\\\ a & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=3$ into $b=3+3a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =3+3(3) \\\\ b & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a-b=3-(12)=-9.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508207 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32fad7a2-8a24-54a3-82c3-95bdccedab06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508183} {:answer/id #uuid "55557865-d7a4-5c61-a72d-2df58ccc52f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508196} {:answer/id #uuid "568a98b9-849b-5575-92e8-a07c6266f271" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508197} {:answer/id #uuid "afc824e1-f2ad-5146-9402-020f186abb13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508226} {:answer/id #uuid "eb4128bc-2e10-521b-aec7-327b7f86a452" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508236}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afc824e1-f2ad-5146-9402-020f186abb13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508226} :answer-field/id #uuid "2074e8b8-4078-53a4-973e-82b464298bff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508178}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7c5faa09-66e6-54c1-b548-04286527c92b" :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $p - q$?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4p &=-24 \\\\ p+5q &=19\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the first equation, we can isolate $p$ by dividing both sides by $4:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4p & =-24 \\\\ p & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $p=-6$ into the second equation and solve for $q:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p+5q & =19 \\\\ (-6)+5q & =19 \\\\ 5q & =25 \\\\ q & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p-q=-6-(5)=-11.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508210 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0095545e-54d6-52cd-924a-d0a5a2f5a1ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508169} {:answer/id #uuid "2f4bd4b3-9bdd-5c11-8b51-838c43d39c9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508180} {:answer/id #uuid "337996a5-122c-53fe-a44a-810d11d9fbdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508184} {:answer/id #uuid "3c4b4903-fe0a-5fb0-a751-3f0fa8df877f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508186} {:answer/id #uuid "6432dee2-0978-5e2c-8294-660f6ce4dc02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508202}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6432dee2-0978-5e2c-8294-660f6ce4dc02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508202} :answer-field/id #uuid "d61ec2e2-631a-51c9-9a12-395b3a9c74bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508231}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "873b7f6f-85bd-5d73-adb8-dc5d593e552e" :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a - b$?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3a-3b &=6 \\\\ -4a+b &=-7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $b$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4a+b & =-7 \\\\ b & =-7+4a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $b=-7+4a$ into the first equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3a-3b & =6 \\\\ -3a-3(-7+4a) & =6 \\\\ -3a+21-12a & =6 \\\\ -15a+21 & =6 \\\\ -15a & =-15 \\\\ a & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=1$ into $b=-7+4a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =-7+4(1) \\\\ b & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a-b=1-(-3)=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508214 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f716510c-61a9-5383-bd22-3d0176b54c16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "201" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508238}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f716510c-61a9-5383-bd22-3d0176b54c16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "201" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508238} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f59436d-c718-5b08-a237-9487d4690290" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508181} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "583c3fbc-a7f5-5eaf-9bde-02befa16b80a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508198}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "583c3fbc-a7f5-5eaf-9bde-02befa16b80a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508198} :answer-field/id #uuid "967e7c7f-52cd-501b-b2ff-8c12483f5017" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508216}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "92720f95-de85-556b-8f87-1b3810fd832e" :question/problem "The coefficients $a$ and $b$ satisfy $b=135-11a.$\n\nThe coefficients $a$ and $b$ also satisfy the equation $7b+162a=435.$ Find the values of $a$ and $b.$\n\n$a\\,=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$b\\,=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "We have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}b &=135-11a \\\\ 7b+162a &=435\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nNotice that the first equation is already solved for $b:$\n\n$$\nb=135-11a\n$$\n\nSo, we replace $b$ in the second equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7b+162a & =435 \\\\ 7(135-11a)+162a & =435 \\\\ 945-77a+162a & =435 \\\\ 945+85a & =435 \\\\ 85a & =-510 \\\\ a & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=-6$ into $b=135-11a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =135-11(-6) \\\\ b & =201\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=-6,\\,b=201.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508215 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a525fbe-b100-56e5-b363-b84bd9a5d52e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508173} {:answer/id #uuid "5b7578d1-6cb2-5958-9c79-b1f69ff339d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508199} {:answer/id #uuid "9fbaa74b-19ed-5c95-b977-ac0cc7054256" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508222} {:answer/id #uuid "b7b07809-444e-59d8-a95b-553b710baa60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508229} {:answer/id #uuid "eac62da3-8a0e-571b-9e13-3d68ba632045" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508235}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a525fbe-b100-56e5-b363-b84bd9a5d52e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508173} :answer-field/id #uuid "97f66384-4244-5039-a3bb-781c22ba011e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508218}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9362a51f-6c19-5264-931e-57aaf13ce3e6" :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a - b$?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2a-4b &=-14 \\\\ -2a+b &=6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $b$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2a+b & =6 \\\\ b & =6+2a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $b=6+2a$ into the first equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2a-4b & =-14 \\\\ -2a-4(6+2a) & =-14 \\\\ -2a-24-8a & =-14 \\\\ -10a-24 & =-14 \\\\ -10a & =10 \\\\ a & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=-1$ into $b=6+2a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =6+2(-1) \\\\ b & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a-b=-1-(4)=-5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508227 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e04510d-2fe1-543a-ac55-911f068010c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508221}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e04510d-2fe1-543a-ac55-911f068010c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508221} :answer-field/id #uuid "496722ff-acc0-5b76-a13e-09917012d73d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508192} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08a38b64-b8c2-526f-8347-6ba7980eb350" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08a38b64-b8c2-526f-8347-6ba7980eb350" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508172} :answer-field/id #uuid "b547fc55-eab5-5d24-ba49-2faa2df55e6a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508228}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "b0966484-f411-5cf8-8677-c24b7843a43c" :question/problem "Find the solution $(x,y)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x-2y &=5 \\\\ 2x+y &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution is $($ {{field-1}} $, $ {{field-2}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+y & =-1 \\\\ y & =-1-2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $y=-1-2x$ into the first equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-2y & =5 \\\\ 5x-2(-1-2x) & =5 \\\\ 5x+2+4x & =5 \\\\ 9x+2 & =5 \\\\ 9x & =3 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $x=\\frac{1}{3}$ into $y=-1-2x,$ we can then find the value of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-1-2\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=\\frac{1}{3},\\,y=-\\frac{5}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508233 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "609dae4d-f20b-597d-8d5c-bd3985bfb3ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508200}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "609dae4d-f20b-597d-8d5c-bd3985bfb3ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508200} :answer-field/id #uuid "313ebe14-9bc4-580a-8ef0-cc446d43568b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508182} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54ede735-9e0a-5b8d-8cb8-1ec5b24e8a75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508195}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54ede735-9e0a-5b8d-8cb8-1ec5b24e8a75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508195} :answer-field/id #uuid "40fbd52d-5989-56ab-8589-60d240620d11" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508190}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ddedcc45-5aba-5229-89b3-d8e7abbe4344" :question/problem "Find the solution $(x,y)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+2y &=12 \\\\ -2x+y &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution is $($ {{field-1}} $, $ {{field-2}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+y & =5 \\\\ y & =5+2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $y=5+2x$ into the first equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+2y & =12 \\\\ 2x+2(5+2x) & =12 \\\\ 2x+10+4x & =12 \\\\ 6x+10 & =12 \\\\ 6x & =2 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $x=\\frac{1}{3}$ into $y=5+2x,$ we can then find the value of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =5+2\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right) \\\\ y & =\\frac{17}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=\\frac{1}{3},\\,y=\\frac{17}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546971 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25d7a53c-5916-5db7-992b-ff7a626a51c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546336} {:answer/id #uuid "51399b6f-2763-5014-9b02-635633f0dada" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546427} {:answer/id #uuid "9e23c320-e17b-534f-8a91-354568ebc163" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546603} {:answer/id #uuid "a3f272eb-ffc1-5fb6-b622-055a0def12d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546617} {:answer/id #uuid "d9f37f2b-79d8-5ebd-8615-8e1bcfb28380" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546732}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9f37f2b-79d8-5ebd-8615-8e1bcfb28380" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546732} :answer-field/id #uuid "78ca5c4c-b502-5598-a6f0-d81d606b319e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546881}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1ad70587-af92-55e0-95cf-31aa82c10e13" :question/math-academy-id "q-52115" :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a-b?$\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}a &=7 \\\\ 3a+6b &=15\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. It so happens that the first equation is already solved for $a:$\n\n$$\na=7\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=7$ into $3a+6b=15,$ then we can find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a+6b & =15 \\\\ 3(7)+6b & =15 \\\\ 6b & =-6 \\\\ b & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=7,\\,b=-1.$ So,\n\n$$\na-b=7-(-1)=7+1=8.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546991 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b85cb2c-460d-5f91-86c0-674d13fae83e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546309} {:answer/id #uuid "242eed59-c937-5dab-b478-b3a1accb9d4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546329} {:answer/id #uuid "463e0a8b-5e11-54a2-8cdd-72b176626176" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546407} {:answer/id #uuid "6a785a85-c477-5db9-a10d-570f963f9181" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546485} {:answer/id #uuid "f5ff80ce-ffb0-542a-ba50-ce8557612884" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546805}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b85cb2c-460d-5f91-86c0-674d13fae83e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546309} :answer-field/id #uuid "e282d81b-1bfe-5c5b-abe6-d91779057814" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546940}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "3b789afd-79c7-56fc-b94a-f894f177dfe2" :question/math-academy-id "q-18555" :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a+b?$\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2b &=6a+14 \\\\ 5b+25 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We number the equations so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2b &=6a+14 && \\,\\,(1) \\\\ 5b+25 &=0. && \\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $(2),$ we can solve for $b$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5b+25 & =0 \\\\ 5b & =-25 \\\\ b & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $b=-5$ into equation $(1)$ and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-5) & =6a+14 \\\\ -10 & =6a+14 \\\\ -10-14 & =6a \\\\ 6a & =-24 \\\\ a & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=-4,\\,b=-5.$ So,\n\n$$\na+b=-4+(-5)=-4-5=-9.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558573 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a889f65-4c3f-5f47-875f-97317df017a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557955}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a889f65-4c3f-5f47-875f-97317df017a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557955} :answer-field/id #uuid "840ece26-ec00-5689-95c2-ab54661da979" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558425} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8d3e3a2-f855-5742-b719-5e9847e96aab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558236}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8d3e3a2-f855-5742-b719-5e9847e96aab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558236} :answer-field/id #uuid "e02a5fd5-c8b7-5c92-871b-d0cf8ac1eaf3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558466}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f2633cd2-d747-5eed-ad0b-333971ef5a97" :question/math-academy-id "q-181154" :question/problem "Consider the following system  of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x &=3 \\\\ x-y &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the solution $(x,y)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$(x,y)=($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. It doesn't matter which equation we pick first, so we choose the easiest one. In this case, the first equation looks like the easiest.\n\nUsing the first equation, we can isolate $x$ by dividing both sides of the equation by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =3 \\\\ x & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $x=\\frac{3}{2}$ into $x-y=1,$ then we can find the value of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-y & =1 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}-y & =1 \\\\ -y & =-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=\\frac{3}{2},\\,y=\\frac{1}{2},$ which can be expressed as $(\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{1}{2}).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562396 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec95d12b-ebdc-5ac8-946c-8865c36899a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562174}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec95d12b-ebdc-5ac8-946c-8865c36899a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562174} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ec83012-bcf1-5281-8dc2-cacc9a39a8f8" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562240} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e269c2f-73d0-5d44-9589-0f161207e171" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561781}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e269c2f-73d0-5d44-9589-0f161207e171" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561781} :answer-field/id #uuid "6fa9b71f-16a8-5365-939e-286334c0da13" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562292}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "0c604a3f-ba93-531d-b858-55cd303f28fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-171693" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-u+v &=-1 \\\\ 3u+3v &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the solution $(u,v)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$(u,v)=($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. It doesn't matter which equation we pick first, so we choose the easiest one. In this case, the first equation looks like the easiest.\n\nUsing the first equation, we can isolate $v$ by adding $u$ to both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\nv=u-1\n$$\n\nSo, we replace $v$ with $u-1$ in the second equation and solve for $u:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3u+3v & =5 \\\\ 3u+3(u-1) & =5 \\\\ 3u+3u-3 & =5 \\\\ 6u & =8 \\\\ u & =\\frac{8}{6} \\\\ u & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $u=\\frac{4}{3}$ into $v=u-1,$ then we can find the value of $v:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u-1 \\\\ v & =\\frac{4}{3}-1 \\\\ v & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $u=\\frac{4}{3},\\,v=\\frac{1}{3},$ which can be expressed as $(\\frac{4}{3},\\frac{1}{3}).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563725 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "283112f9-9ffe-5a11-bbfc-a5ba098b6d08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563035}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "283112f9-9ffe-5a11-bbfc-a5ba098b6d08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563035} :answer-field/id #uuid "152e2f23-0e18-55aa-a6f1-c39bead952a2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563528} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "967fdc49-d3aa-54f3-af09-6a561f202139" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "360" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563279}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "967fdc49-d3aa-54f3-af09-6a561f202139" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "360" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563279} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee0751b7-37b1-5581-b463-69aae210a148" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563635}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b42bde79-43e7-5e0d-aa7f-ed2b4b36837d" :question/math-academy-id "q-167218" :question/problem "The coefficients $a$ and $b$ also satisfy the equation $100a+15b=4\\,800.$ Find the values of $a$ and $b.$\n\n$a\\,=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$b\\,=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "We have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}b &=270-15a \\\\ 100a+15b &=4\\,800\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nNotice that the first equation is already solved for $b:$\n\n$$\nb=270-15a\n$$\n\nSo, we replace $b$ in the second equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}100a+15b & =4\\,800 \\\\ 100a+15(270-15a) & =4\\,800 \\\\ 100a+4\\,050-225a & =4\\,800 \\\\ -125a+4\\,050 & =4\\,800 \\\\ -125a & =750 \\\\ a & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=-6$ into $b=270-15a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =270-15(-6) \\\\ b & =360\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=-6,\\,b=360.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186615453 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e6b9abf-1cbf-53d7-996b-eb36670ba625" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186614907}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e6b9abf-1cbf-53d7-996b-eb36670ba625" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186614907} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e3d5755-cc9c-528a-bbfa-e29af0e9f3d9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615206} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3cf005a-7035-5c9e-9acb-73258df41c2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "540" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615169}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3cf005a-7035-5c9e-9acb-73258df41c2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "540" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615169} :answer-field/id #uuid "66edf6a7-fca7-517d-ab71-81772ac1bcd0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615265}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c8ee6fd9-a041-550d-99fe-b688d795469d" :question/math-academy-id "q-135291" :question/problem "Mary wonders where and when they'd met if Sam left home $3.8$ minutes earlier and walked with a speed of $50$ meters per minute. She finds that the distance $d$ from home they'd meet can be modeled using the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}d+60t &=960 \\\\ d-50t &=190.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time (in minutes) since Mary left the community park.\n\nMary and Sam would meet$\\,$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$minutes after Mary left the community park.\n\nMary and Sam would meet at a distance of $\\,$\n{{field-2}}$\\,$meters from home." :question/worked-solution "To solve the given system of linear equations, we will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. It doesn't matter which equation we pick first, so we choose the easiest one. In this case, the second equation looks like the easiest.\n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $d$ adding to both sides of the equation $50t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d-50t &=190 \\\\ d &=190+50t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we replace $d$ with $190+50t$ in the first equation and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d+60t=960 \\\\ (190+50t)+60t & =960 \\\\ 190+110t & =960 \\\\ 110t & =960-190 \\\\ 110t & =770 \\\\ t & =\\frac{770}{110} \\\\ t & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, they would have met after $t=7$ minutes.\n\nIf we substitute $t=7$ into $d=190+50t$, we can find the value of $d:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =190+50t \\\\  & =190+50(7) \\\\  & =540\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, they meet at a distance of $540$ meters from home."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632865 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22fb1199-a8f0-5ba3-94c1-4fe54d00c477" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632860} {:answer/id #uuid "6217ce4c-5c47-5321-95eb-bd7ed318fcb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632870} {:answer/id #uuid "ded7b2d4-2232-5456-b8ad-a4e09a853dec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632882} {:answer/id #uuid "ebbc63a2-4bd6-5d1a-b89a-9756ed93e87e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632886} {:answer/id #uuid "ede9003c-dadb-5026-89b2-5630fe838c1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632887}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ebbc63a2-4bd6-5d1a-b89a-9756ed93e87e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632886} :answer-field/id #uuid "8039fd02-8d24-5a9b-b27f-0359bfbc4263" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632874}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4681a163-40e5-5445-ba23-6f719a7705fb" :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $p - q$?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5p &=-10 \\\\ p+5q &=-17\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the first equation, we can isolate $p$ by dividing both sides by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5p & =-10 \\\\ p & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $p=-2$ into the second equation and solve for $q:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p+5q & =-17 \\\\ (-2)+5q & =-17 \\\\ 5q & =-15 \\\\ q & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $p=-2,\\,q=-3.$ So,\n\n$$\np - q=-2-(-3)=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632873 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2afa4594-0335-50c5-baf9-664062a5c525" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632861} {:answer/id #uuid "4f367be5-8de1-5871-a02e-1b656ea3fefd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632867} {:answer/id #uuid "5b7ec00d-6501-5a55-be33-d2799bc9f7a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632869} {:answer/id #uuid "c269ed65-46a6-5d56-bfb3-1ce57809c38c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632881} {:answer/id #uuid "f30c0ef4-c880-5bf9-bb4f-0c70fbceb929" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632888}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f30c0ef4-c880-5bf9-bb4f-0c70fbceb929" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632888} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9283a90-adb3-5f67-a506-4b57d81a5a33" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632879}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7e66cc4a-738d-5443-ad33-daca77ff4c3c" :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a - b$?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5b-3a &=8 \\\\ -4b+a &=-5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $a$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4b+a & =-5 \\\\ a & =-5+4b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $a=-5+4b$ into the first equation and solve for $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5b-3a & =8 \\\\ 5b-3(-5+4b) & =8 \\\\ 5b+15-12b & =8 \\\\ -7b+15 & =8 \\\\ -7b & =-7 \\\\ b & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $b=1$ into $a=-5+4b,$ we can then find the value of $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =-5+4(1) \\\\ a & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $a=-1,\\,b=1.$ So,\n\n$$\na - b=-1-(1)=-2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632876 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5ab13a8-66eb-5f89-87d2-4dc2e894cd63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632884}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5ab13a8-66eb-5f89-87d2-4dc2e894cd63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632884} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c7eaa2a-2e05-5957-b576-035c3e2194b2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632866} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "527b7232-1fd3-5f24-8b9a-6dc937d1b4ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632868}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "527b7232-1fd3-5f24-8b9a-6dc937d1b4ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632868} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a45341e-4f36-5abf-a9a6-6893f30dba17" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632875}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8bff0e3e-2036-5666-b7ce-75fff614792d" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6y &=-16 \\\\ -3y+2x &=6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the solution $(x,y)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$(x,y)=($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the first equation, we can isolate $y$ by dividing both sides of the equation by $6:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6y & =-16 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $y=-\\frac{8}{3}$ into $-3y+2x=6,$ then we can find the value of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3y+2x & =6 \\\\ -3\\left(-\\frac{8}{3}\\right)+2x & =6 \\\\ 2x & =-2 \\\\ x & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $y=-\\frac{8}{3},\\,x=-1.$ This can be expressed as $(-1,-\\frac{8}{3}).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632885 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "037c70e5-a983-5572-b6d3-5cc94661b5f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632859} {:answer/id #uuid "2e525041-d058-5e66-aced-f9a7fde2bdbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632862} {:answer/id #uuid "45ba51a6-fd9f-5cb6-b315-4f4b80cf3ab3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632864} {:answer/id #uuid "9250ac5e-9551-5d92-93ae-08119ebf3678" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632877} {:answer/id #uuid "aa388d1f-eb45-543c-8500-78b2d834ded1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632880}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "037c70e5-a983-5572-b6d3-5cc94661b5f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632859} :answer-field/id #uuid "6884345f-7143-5288-86d5-41f229b50f00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632871}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e90ed6dd-ee30-50f3-a3fd-20d23f868838" :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a - b$?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2a+b &=-5 \\\\ -5a+3b &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the first equation, we can isolate $b$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a+b & =-5 \\\\ b & =-5-2a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $b=-5-2a$ into the second equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5a+3b & =-4 \\\\ -5a+3(-5-2a) & =-4 \\\\ -5a-15-6a & =-4 \\\\ -11a-15 & =-4 \\\\ -11a & =11 \\\\ a & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=-1$ into $b=-5-2a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =-5-2(-1) \\\\ b & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $a=-1,\\,b=-3.$ So,\n\n$$\na - b=-1-(-3)=2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632889 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ab5b2e8-ff3f-58ad-b87f-97436a6f302f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632863}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ab5b2e8-ff3f-58ad-b87f-97436a6f302f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632863} :answer-field/id #uuid "75854c12-cbb9-50e0-9a24-ea7ab1e94712" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632872} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0906662-2393-5770-881f-a38e5d6e5f45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632883}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0906662-2393-5770-881f-a38e5d6e5f45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632883} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1af3caf-0d3f-596f-a658-2d9c68a81ed0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632878}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "fad041ba-7ce4-5b1b-8161-a125b46a6d63" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4y &=-2 \\\\ -2y+x &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the solution $(x,y)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$(x,y)=($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the first equation, we can isolate $y$ by dividing both sides of the equation by $4:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4y & =-2 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $y=-\\frac{1}{2}$ into $-2y+x=2,$ then we can find the value of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2y+x & =2 \\\\ -2\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)+x & =2 \\\\ x & =1 \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $y=-\\frac{1}{2},\\,x=1.$ This can be expressed as $(1,-\\frac{1}{2}).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186633656 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "769223b4-058d-51dd-92ab-34cfff258702" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186633666}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "769223b4-058d-51dd-92ab-34cfff258702" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186633666} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce172f0d-a912-59d0-afc0-1ed720436bf8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186633672} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "488c196c-717d-5ba3-a4a5-1f7ecb2fc497" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186633659}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "488c196c-717d-5ba3-a4a5-1f7ecb2fc497" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186633659} :answer-field/id #uuid "d417ddaa-0113-57df-bfbd-5e6059a818cf" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186633674}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1d32c422-3e67-5367-8644-b7d6ffb19b9f" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2p + 3q &=-1 \\\\ 4p - 4q + 4 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the solution $(p,q)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$(p,q)=($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "We number the equations so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2p + 3q &=-1 && (1) \\\\ 4p - 4q + 4 &=0 && (2)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $(2)$, we can solve for $q$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} -4q + 4p &= -4 \\\\ -4q &= -4p - 4 \\\\ q &= p + 1 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $q=p + 1$ into equation $(1)$ and solve for $p$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 3q - 2p + 1 &= 0 \\\\ 3\\left(p + 1\\right) - 2p + 1 &= 0 \\\\ 3p + 3 - 2p + 1 &= 0 \\\\ p &= -4 \\\\ p &= -4 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $p=-4$ back into equation $(2)$, then we can find the value of $q$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} -4q + 4\\left(-4\\right) &= -4 \\\\ -4q - 16 &= -4 \\\\ -4q &= 12 \\\\ q &= -3 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $p=-4,\\,q=-3$, which can be expressed as $(-4,-3)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186633657 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "955dddb8-26f6-56d1-acfe-2f5e5fca35a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186633669}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "955dddb8-26f6-56d1-acfe-2f5e5fca35a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186633669} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e064604-1ffb-5323-bc83-d5781d1d4ccf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186633664} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "052632d1-feb3-576b-95b1-02262d14ab23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186633652}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "052632d1-feb3-576b-95b1-02262d14ab23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186633652} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1b85c1f-c747-56ca-b5d8-c5edf6be0820" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186633673}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "25e9fd42-3c14-53a8-b55e-66ddee0643b9" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-9u - 3v &=-18 \\\\ -4u - 4v + 8 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the solution $(u,v)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$(u,v)=($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "We number the equations so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-9u - 3v &=-18 && (1) \\\\ -4u - 4v + 8 &=0 && (2)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $(1)$, we can solve for $v$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} -3v - 9u &= -18 \\\\ -3v &= 9u - 18 \\\\ v &= -3u + 6 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $v=-3u + 6$ into equation $(2)$ and solve for $u$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} -4v - 4u + 8 &= 0 \\\\ -4\\left(-3u + 6\\right) - 4u + 8 &= 0 \\\\ 12u - 24 - 4u + 8 &= 0 \\\\ 8u &= 16 \\\\ u &= 2 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $u=2$ back into equation $(1)$, then we can find the value of $v$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} -3v - 9\\left(2\\right) &= -18 \\\\ -3v - 18 &= -18 \\\\ -3v &= 0 \\\\ v &= 0 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $u=2,\\,v=0$, which can be expressed as $(2,0)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186633658 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cb6ceec-9f89-5598-8cb1-fbf211c3cbf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186633654}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0cb6ceec-9f89-5598-8cb1-fbf211c3cbf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186633654} :answer-field/id #uuid "747eed39-aa71-5f18-9314-30fdb6818cf8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186633665} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14dd4a36-3c19-5c63-9b84-f13137881a5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186633655}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14dd4a36-3c19-5c63-9b84-f13137881a5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186633655} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6354578-99b1-57ad-99fa-fb1b9e2f62bc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186633670}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2a5be942-1c27-5810-a419-5e2776ac35d3" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x - 9y &=-36 \\\\ -7x - 4y - 1 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the solution $(x,y)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$(x,y)=($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "We number the equations so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x - 9y &=-36 && (1) \\\\ -7x - 4y - 1 &=0 && (2)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $(1)$, we can solve for $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} -3x - 9y &= -36 \\\\ -3x &= 9y - 36 \\\\ x &= -3y + 12 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=-3y + 12$ into equation $(2)$ and solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} -7x - 4y - 1 &= 0 \\\\ -7\\left(-3y + 12\\right) - 4y - 1 &= 0 \\\\ 21y - 84 - 4y - 1 &= 0 \\\\ 17y &= 85 \\\\ y &= 5 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $y=5$ back into equation $(1)$, then we can find the value of $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} -3x - 9\\left(5\\right) &= -36 \\\\ -3x - 45 &= -36 \\\\ -3x &= 9 \\\\ x &= -3 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-3,\\,y=5$, which can be expressed as $(-3,5)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186633675 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65c0bf5b-7790-553b-ae77-7cc6133b7216" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186633663}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65c0bf5b-7790-553b-ae77-7cc6133b7216" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186633663} :answer-field/id #uuid "51eb11dd-031f-5ef0-bede-55b7489e965a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186633660} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e3121c4-eae4-5b46-b988-bfc00a198226" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186633668}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e3121c4-eae4-5b46-b988-bfc00a198226" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186633668} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c97d468-1c27-5515-b306-e52589b21e91" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186633661}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ed72f62d-e95c-5059-995c-045117f363d6" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4a + 4b &=24 \\\\ 4a - 2b - 6 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the solution $(a,b)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$(a,b)=($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "We number the equations so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4a + 4b &=24 && (1) \\\\ 4a - 2b - 6 &=0 && (2)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $(2)$, we can solve for $b$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} -2b + 4a &= 6 \\\\ -2b &= -4a + 6 \\\\ b &= 2a - 3 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $b=2a - 3$ into equation $(1)$ and solve for $a$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 4b + 4a - 24 &= 0 \\\\ 4\\left(2a - 3\\right) + 4a - 24 &= 0 \\\\ 8a - 12 + 4a - 24 &= 0 \\\\ 12a &= 36 \\\\ a &= 3 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=3$ back into equation $(2)$, then we can find the value of $b$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} -2b + 4\\left(3\\right) &= 6 \\\\ -2b + 12 &= 6 \\\\ -2b &= -6 \\\\ b &= 3 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=3,\\,b=3$, which can be expressed as $(3,3)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186633676 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f9cb69b-af95-5337-a909-d889171464bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186633662}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f9cb69b-af95-5337-a909-d889171464bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186633662} :answer-field/id #uuid "095c04dd-bfe5-56d2-82b5-c87e3b3a3cde" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186633653} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d1d4d5c-e2cf-531b-b07a-4f624ec2c5e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186633667}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d1d4d5c-e2cf-531b-b07a-4f624ec2c5e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186633667} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab692471-e7c5-5429-a826-31c006ea5435" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186633671}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f37c1490-6c34-5fa1-9324-27cb43627b98" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3p + 6q &=-12 \\\\ 5p - 3q + 20 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the solution $(p,q)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$(p,q)=($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "We number the equations so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3p + 6q &=-12 && (1) \\\\ 5p - 3q + 20 &=0 && (2)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $(1)$, we can solve for $p$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 3p + 6q &= -12 \\\\ 3p &= -6q - 12 \\\\ p &= -2q - 4 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $p=-2q - 4$ into equation $(2)$ and solve for $q$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 5p - 3q + 20 &= 0 \\\\ 5\\left(-2q - 4\\right) - 3q + 20 &= 0 \\\\ -10q - 20 - 3q + 20 &= 0 \\\\ -13q &= 0 \\\\ q &= 0 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $q=0$ back into equation $(1)$, then we can find the value of $p$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 3p + 6\\left(0\\right) &= -12 \\\\ 3p &= -12 \\\\ 3p &= -12 \\\\ p &= -4 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $p=-4,\\,q=0$, which can be expressed as $(-4,0)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186664095 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "441433e9-0217-5b65-89b5-e4356edfa0e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1912" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186663635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "441433e9-0217-5b65-89b5-e4356edfa0e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1912" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186663635} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c516232-d44c-53e0-b4f2-81d942c66268" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186663981} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d8b68470-160d-5f41-a127-282cce8c75f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "166" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186663875}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8b68470-160d-5f41-a127-282cce8c75f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "166" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186663875} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c3c7cb2-6b55-50a9-9e14-80acc4ace6f1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186663996}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b1f360f1-f3d1-50a0-9490-2c171ed25df8" :question/math-academy-id "q-138797" :question/problem "![](images/ff/ff3a9b43deb13eb7ffdc3c8f1ac918c8ea1925c49418fc25038179e993de6093.png)\n\nThe total cost and revenue per month (in dollars) of the restaurant can be modeled by the equations $y=750+7x$ and $y=11x+86,$ respectively, where $x$ is the number of units sold. \n\nSolve the system below using the substitution method to find the exact number of units that need to be produced to break even and the revenue generated at this point.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=750+7x \\\\ y &=86+11x\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n**Note**: A company breaks even when the total revenue equals the total cost and is represented by the intersection of the revenue and cost functions.\n\nThe restaurant breaks even when$\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\,$units are produced. \n\nThe revenue generated when selling this number of units is$\\,$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\,$dollars." :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nNotice that $y$ is isolated in the first equation. Therefore, we can replace $y$ with $750+7x$ in the second equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =86+11x \\\\ 750+7x & =86+11x \\\\ 750+7x-7x & =86+11x-7x \\\\ 750 & =86+4x \\\\ 750-86 & =86+4x-86 \\\\ 664 & =4x \\\\ \\frac{664}{4} & =\\frac{4x}{4} \\\\ 166 & =x \\\\ x & =166\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $x=166$ into $y=86+11x$, then we can find the value of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &=86+11(166)=1\\,912\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the solution to the system of equations is $x=166$ and $y=1\\,912.$\nTherefore, the restaurant breaks even when $166$ units are produced, and the revenue generated when selling this number of units is $\\$1\\,912.$"}]}
